   "confidence": "low",
   "notes": "Victorian Gothic front of yellow gault brick with Ketton-stone dressings (White Stuff: green hanging sign and vertical green banner). Ground floor of tall pointed-arch openings on clustered stone shafts with carved capitals (shop windows plus a pointed-arch entrance at the south end next to Whistles); first floor has a corbelled stone oriel with traceried parapet and lancet lights; pointed lancet sashes above; corbel-table eaves. CAVEAT: the gothic building looks about 10 m wide (it also includes a rounded corner oriel/turret with a conical slate roof at its north end), but this OSM wall is only 6.5 m and there is a 4.5 m gap to wall 13, so the north corner bay probably belongs to the unmapped 11-12; I annotated only the southern bays, so element positions are rough."
